# Ticket dossiers — {{ project_name }}

One file per ticket, written during Step 2 of `ticket-intake`, before any case is
authored. A dossier is the evidence of what was actually read: the ticket, its comments,
attachments, pull requests and linked tickets.

- File name: `<TICKET-KEY>.md`, copied from `TEMPLATE.md`
- Every fact carries its source (ticket field, comment author + date, PR number, file
  name, linked key)
- Links that could not be fetched are recorded as `NOT FOUND`; files that could not be
  opened as `NOT OPENED`. A dossier never contains a summary of something the agent did
  not read
- Dossiers are committed. When cases look wrong, the dossier is the first thing to audit

Later skills (`gap-analysis`, `verify-ticket`) read the dossier instead of re-fetching
the ticket.
